IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- North Dakota Century Code chapter 57-38 (income tax) -- what an individual meets: who is a resident (s 57-38-01(11)); who
-- must file and by when, and paying the tax (ss 57-38-31(1), 57-38-34(2), 57-38-35); reporting federal changes
-- (s 57-38-34.4); North Dakota taxable income from federal taxable income (s 57-38-30.3(2), the subtractions in (a), (d),
-- (g), (r), (s) computed and the rest as inputs); the tax (s 57-38-30.3(1)(a)-(d), with the Tax Commissioner's indexed
-- schedules under (1)(g)); and the marriage penalty credit (s 57-38-01.28).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer. "Am I a North Dakota resident? Must I file? By when? How much North Dakota tax do I pay?"
-- Provisions addressed to the Tax Commissioner are encoded as what they mean for that person: the schedules the
-- commissioner prescribes in place of those in the text (s 57-38-30.3(1)(g)), the indexed maximum marriage penalty credit.
--
-- Edition: N.D.C.C. ch. 57-38, the Legislative Council's 07/01/25 update (all changes of the 69th Legislative Assembly,
-- 2025 session), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ndcc-t57c38.txt.
--
-- Federal taxable income, federal AGI, the IRC s 86 social security amount, the federal filing status and filing
-- requirement are inputs. Read with the federal Internal Revenue Code encoding (subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/);
-- cross-folder IMPORT is not possible in the stable l4.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: part-year residents and nonresidents (s 57-38-30.3(1)(f): `not covered`); estates and trusts ((1)(e));
-- the farm income averaging election ((9)); every credit in s 57-38-30.3(7) except the marriage penalty credit; the
-- credit for tax paid to another state ((4)); the adjustments of s 57-38-30.3(2) other than (a), (d), (e), (g), (r), (s)
-- (inputs); estimated tax (s 57-38-62 and on), interest and penalties (s 57-38-45).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `North Dakota Century Code chapter 57-38 -- individual income tax`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the tax of an individual who is not a resident for the entire year is prorated under s 57-38-30.3(1)(f), which is not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` x y MEANS IF x AT LEAST y THEN x ELSE y

§§ `s 57-38-01(11) -- am I a resident`

-- s 57-38-01(11): "'Resident' applies only to natural persons and includes ... any person domiciled in the state of North
-- Dakota and any other person who maintains a permanent place of abode within the state and spends in the aggregate more
-- than seven months of the income year within the state."
GIVEN `domiciled in North Dakota` IS A BOOLEAN
      `maintains a permanent place of abode in North Dakota` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months of the year spent in North Dakota` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a resident` IF
        `domiciled in North Dakota`
    OR  (    `maintains a permanent place of abode in North Dakota`
         AND `months of the year spent in North Dakota` GREATER THAN 7)

§§ `ss 57-38-31, 57-38-34, 57-38-35, 57-38-34.4 -- filing, paying and reporting`

-- s 57-38-31(1): "Every resident individual ... who is required by the provisions of the United States Internal Revenue Code
-- ... to file a federal income tax return, and every individual or fiduciary who receives income derived from sources in
-- this state, shall file an income tax return with the state tax commissioner".
GIVEN `resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `required to file a federal return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives income from North Dakota sources` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must file a North Dakota return under s 57-38-31(1)` IF
        (`resident` AND `required to file a federal return`)
    OR  `receives income from North Dakota sources`

-- s 57-38-34(2): "Returns made on the basis of the calendar year must be filed on or before the fifteenth day of April
-- following the close of the calendar year". s 57-38-35: "Every taxpayer shall compute the amount of tax due under the
-- return and shall attach thereto" payment "for the amount of the tax computed" -- so the tax is paid with the return.
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the due date for a calendar-year return` `tax year` MEANS Date 15 4 (`tax year` PLUS 1)

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the tax commissioner`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `file the return`
    `pay the tax computed on the return`
    `report the federal change by an amended state return`
    `file an amended state return with a copy of the amended federal return`

-- The duty to file, and to pay with the return, counted in days from the close of the calendar year (31 December).
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to file and pay` `tax year` MEANS
        (PARTY `the taxpayer`
         MUST  `file the return`
         WITHIN (`the due date for a calendar-year return` `tax year`) MINUS (Date 31 12 `tax year`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "no return filed by 15 April after the calendar year (s 57-38-34(2))")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the taxpayer`
         MUST  `pay the tax computed on the return`
         WITHIN (`the due date for a calendar-year return` `tax year`) MINUS (Date 31 12 `tax year`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "tax not paid with the return (s 57-38-35)")

-- s 57-38-34.4: "(1) If a person's federal taxable income or federal income tax liability for any taxable year is changed or
-- corrected by the United States internal revenue service, or other competent authority, the person shall report the
-- changes or corrections within ninety days after the date of the final determination of them by filing an amended state
-- income tax return ..." "(2) ... if a person files an amended federal income tax return ..., the person shall file an
-- amended state income tax return and a copy of the amended federal income tax return within ninety days after the amended
-- federal income tax return is filed." Days run from the final determination, or from the amended federal filing.
DECLARE `Federal change` IS ONE OF
    `changed or corrected by the IRS or other competent authority`
    `an amended federal return I filed`

GIVEN `change` IS A `Federal change`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to report a federal change` `change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `change`
    WHEN `changed or corrected by the IRS or other competent authority` THEN
        PARTY `the taxpayer`
        MUST  `report the federal change by an amended state return`
        WITHIN 90
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "federal change not reported within ninety days of the final determination (s 57-38-34.4(1))"
    WHEN `an amended federal return I filed` THEN
        PARTY `the taxpayer`
        MUST  `file an amended state return with a copy of the amended federal return`
        WITHIN 90
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "no amended state return within ninety days of the amended federal return (s 57-38-34.4(2))"

GIVEN `the day the change became final or the amended federal return was filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to report a federal change` `the day the change became final or the amended federal return was filed` MEANS
    `the day the change became final or the amended federal return was filed` PLUS 90

§§ `s 57-38-30.3(2) -- North Dakota taxable income`

-- s 57-38-30.3(2): "'North Dakota taxable income' means the federal taxable income of an individual ... adjusted as follows:"
-- (a) "Reduced by interest income from obligations of the United States and income exempt from state income tax under
-- federal statute or United States or North Dakota constitutional provisions";
-- (d) "Reduced by forty percent of: (1) The excess of the taxpayer's net long-term capital gain for the taxable year over the
-- net short-term capital loss for that year ... allowed only to the extent the net long-term capital gain is allocated to
-- this state. (2) Qualified dividends ... but only if taxed at a federal income tax rate that is lower than the regular
-- federal income tax rates" (the 30%-of-all-dividends alternative is not encoded);
-- (e) "Increased by the amount of a lump sum distribution for which income averaging was elected under section 402";
-- (g) "Reduced by the amount of military pay received by a taxpayer as a member of the armed forces ... on federal active
-- duty, member of the national guard or reserve member";
-- (r) "Reduced by the amount received by a taxpayer as retired military personnel benefits";
-- (s) "Reduced by the amount of social security benefits included in a taxpayer's federal adjusted gross income under
-- section 86 of the Internal Revenue Code."
-- Other reductions and increases are inputs.
GIVEN `net long-term capital gain over net short-term capital loss, allocated to North Dakota` IS A NUMBER
      `qualified dividends taxed federally at the lower rates, allocated to North Dakota` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 57-38-30.3(2)(d) reduction` MEANS
    40% TIMES (`the greater of` 0 `net long-term capital gain over net short-term capital loss, allocated to North Dakota` PLUS `qualified dividends taxed federally at the lower rates, allocated to North Dakota`)

GIVEN `federal taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `US obligation interest and other federally exempt income` IS A NUMBER
      `the (d) capital gain and dividend reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `lump sum distribution averaged under IRC s 402` IS A NUMBER
      `military pay` IS A NUMBER
      `retired military personnel benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `social security in federal AGI under IRC s 86` IS A NUMBER
      `other reductions` IS A NUMBER
      `other increases` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`North Dakota taxable income` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0
        (  `federal taxable income`
         PLUS (`lump sum distribution averaged under IRC s 402` PLUS `other increases`)
         MINUS (    `US obligation interest and other federally exempt income`
               PLUS `the (d) capital gain and dividend reduction`
               PLUS `military pay`
               PLUS `retired military personnel benefits`
               PLUS `social security in federal AGI under IRC s 86`
               PLUS `other reductions`))

§§ `s 57-38-30.3(1) -- the tax`

-- s 57-38-30.3(1): "The tax for individuals is equal to North Dakota taxable income multiplied by the rates in the applicable
-- rate schedule in subdivisions a through d corresponding to an individual's filing status used for federal income tax
-- purposes." Each schedule has three rows: 0.00% to a first figure, 1.95% to a second, 2.50% above it. (3): "The same filing
-- status used when filing federal income tax returns must be used".
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `single`
    `married filing jointly`
    `surviving spouse`
    `married filing separately`
    `head of household`

-- A schedule is fixed by its two figures, because the rates "may not be changed" ((1)(g)).
DECLARE `Schedule` HAS
    `top of the 0.00% bracket` IS A NUMBER
    `top of the 1.95% bracket` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Schedule`
`schedule` a b MEANS `Schedule` WITH `top of the 0.00% bracket` IS a, `top of the 1.95% bracket` IS b

-- (1)(a) single: $44,725 / $225,975; (b) married filing jointly and surviving spouse: $74,750 / $275,100; (c) married
-- filing separately: $37,375 / $137,550; (d) head of household: $59,950 / $250,550.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A `Schedule`
`the schedule in the Century Code` `status` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `single`                    THEN `schedule` 44725 225975
    WHEN `married filing jointly`    THEN `schedule` 74750 275100
    WHEN `surviving spouse`          THEN `schedule` 74750 275100
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `schedule` 37375 137550
    WHEN `head of household`         THEN `schedule` 59950 250550

-- Each row reads "$B + R% of amount over $X". The top row's base is 1.95% of the width of the middle bracket: $3,534.38 for
-- single is 1.95% of $181,250 ($3,534.375) rounded to the cent. The encoding computes the base exactly (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `s` IS A `Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on a schedule` `taxable income` `s` MEANS
    LET a MEANS s's `top of the 0.00% bracket`
        b MEANS s's `top of the 1.95% bracket`
    IN BRANCH
        IF `taxable income` AT MOST a THEN 0
        IF `taxable income` AT MOST b THEN 1.95% TIMES (`taxable income` MINUS a)
        OTHERWISE (1.95% TIMES (b MINUS a)) PLUS (2.50% TIMES (`taxable income` MINUS b))

-- (1)(f): "For an individual who is not a resident of this state for the entire year ... the tax is equal to the tax
-- otherwise computed under this subsection multiplied by a fraction" -- not encoded.
GIVEN `resident for the entire year` IS A BOOLEAN, `taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `s` IS A `Schedule`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the s 57-38-30.3 tax` `resident for the entire year` `taxable income` `s` MEANS
    IF `resident for the entire year`
    THEN `answered` (`the tax on a schedule` `taxable income` `s`)
    ELSE `not covered` `the tax of an individual who is not a resident for the entire year is prorated under s 57-38-30.3(1)(f), which is not encoded`

§§ `s 57-38-01.28 -- the marriage penalty credit`

-- s 57-38-01.28(1): "A married couple filing a joint return ... is allowed a credit of not to exceed three hundred dollars per
-- couple"; the commissioner "shall adjust the maximum amount" with the rate schedules (an input). (2): "the difference between
-- the tax on the couple's joint North Dakota taxable income under the rates and income levels in subdivision b ... and the
-- sum of the tax under the rates and income levels of subdivision a ... on the qualified income of the lesser-earning
-- spouse, and the tax under ... subdivision a ... on the couple's joint North Dakota taxable income, minus the qualified
-- income of the lesser-earning spouse." (4)(a): qualifying income is earned income (IRC s 32(c)(2)) and pension and annuity
-- income included in North Dakota taxable income; (4)(b): the lesser-earning spouse's is reduced by "the amount for one
-- exemption under section 151(d)" and "one-half of the amount of the standard deduction under section 63(c)(2)(A) (4)" of
-- the IRC (federal amounts, inputs; NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `joint taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `lesser-earning spouse's qualifying income` IS A NUMBER
      `the IRC s 151(d) exemption amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the IRC s 63(c)(2)(A) standard deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum credit` IS A NUMBER
      `joint schedule` IS A `Schedule`
      `single schedule` IS A `Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the marriage penalty credit` `joint taxable income` `lesser-earning spouse's qualifying income` `the IRC s 151(d) exemption amount` `the IRC s 63(c)(2)(A) standard deduction` `the maximum credit` `joint schedule` `single schedule` MEANS
    LET q MEANS `the lesser of` `joint taxable income`
                    (`the greater of` 0 (`lesser-earning spouse's qualifying income` MINUS (`the IRC s 151(d) exemption amount` PLUS (`the IRC s 63(c)(2)(A) standard deduction` DIVIDED BY 2))))
        `joint tax` MEANS `the tax on a schedule` `joint taxable income` `joint schedule`
        `two singles` MEANS (`the tax on a schedule` q `single schedule`) PLUS (`the tax on a schedule` (`joint taxable income` MINUS q) `single schedule`)
    IN `the lesser of` `the maximum credit` (`the greater of` 0 (`joint tax` MINUS `two singles`))
